 peptides corresponding to the sequences 1&#x02013;45 and 46&#x02013;96 of the prohormone</article-title><source><italic>Hoppe-Seyler&#x02019;s Zeitschrift f&#x000fc;r Physiologische Chemie</italic></source><year>1980</year><volume>361</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>857</fpage><lpage>863</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tager</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name><name><surname>Steiner</surname><given-names>DF</given-names></name><name><surname>Patzelt</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Biosynthesis of insulin and glucagon</article-title><source><italic>Methods in Cell Biology</italic></source><year>1981</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>73</fpage><lpage>88</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7035811</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goeddel</surname><given-names>DV</given-names></name><name><surname>Kleid</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name><name><surname>Bolivar</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Expression in Escherichia coli of chemically synthesized genes for human insulin</article-title><source><italic>Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America</italic></source><year>1979</year><volume>76</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>106</fpage><lpage>110</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">85300</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>WL</given-names></name><name><surname>Baxter</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Recombinant DNA&#x02014;a new source of insulin</article-title><source><italic>Diabetologia</italic></source><year>1980</year><volume>18</volu